2. **Using `React.cloneElement`:**

`React.cloneElement` is used when you want to modify the existing children of a component. It creates a new React element with the same type as the old one, but with the new props you provide.

```jsx
function MyComponentWithChildren(props) {
  return React.Children.map(props.children, child =>
    React.cloneElement(child, { someNewProp: true })
  );
}

// Usage
