  <div className="child1">Child 1</div>
  <div className="child2">Child 2</div>
</MyComponentWithChildren>
```

In the example above, `MyComponentWithChildren` receives the children as an array, and for each child, it creates a new element with the same type but with an additional prop `someNewProp: true`.

In summary, use `React.cloneElement` when you need to modify the existing children of a component, and pass properties directly when you just want to provide new props to a component.

